The patient awoke from sedation without any significant nausea or discomfort. She tolerated sips of water well and had stable vitals (BP: 120/78, HR: 74, SpO2: 98%). Diet/Activity: Resume normal diet as tolerated. Avoid alcohol and heavy meals for the remainder of the day. Activities as tolerated, but avoid driving or operating heavy machinery for 24 hours.

Results Communication: Results of the examination and further recommendations will be communicated via phone or patient portal within 2 weeks.

